/-!
# Geometric assembly of the opposite centralizer selection

The assembly constructs every field of the selected critical placement from
escape of the original local orbit and a cover by its good conjugates and
the incident radius group. The bad-conjugate span and its literal product
with that radius group are also retained for the source calculation.

The unconditional `pathPlacement_nonempty` remains to be assembled after
proving those two mathematical inputs from the original frame and edge data.
No existence or spanning assertion is included in their definitions.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), (4.4.1)(1), printed p.891.
-/
